{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y_safestan_flat`, a deterministic row-major flattening of the original response array `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: the original likelihood scored indexed slices `y[i]` inside a loop, which is not allowed for protected data in SafeStan. The rewrite adds `y_safestan_flat`, with `y_safestan_flat[(i - 1) * J + j] = y[i, j]`, builds the matching linear predictor vector in the model block after the parameter priors, and observes `y_safestan_flat` once with a plain built-in `bernoulli_logit` sampling statement. The priors on `theta` and `b` were already explicit built-in priors and are preserved unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"//# ---- irt-1pl-vague-stan ----
data {
  int<lower=0> I;
  int<lower=0> J;
  array[I, J] int<lower=0, upper=1> y;
  array[I * J] int<lower=0, upper=1> y_safestan_flat;
  real mu_theta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_theta;
  real mu_b;
  real<lower=0> sigma_b;
}
parameters {
  vector[I] b;
  vector[J] theta;
}
model {
  vector[I * J] eta_safestan_flat;

  theta ~ normal(mu_theta, sigma_theta);
  b ~ normal(mu_b, sigma_b);

  for (i in 1 : I) {
    for (j in 1 : J) {
      eta_safestan_flat[(i - 1) * J + j] = theta[j] - b[i];
    }
  }
  y_safestan_flat ~ bernoulli_logit(eta_safestan_flat);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"I":2,"J":3,"mu_b":2.6087365806619434,"mu_theta":2.763958451958236,"sigma_b":1.7370455838133922,"sigma_theta":1.210515773341465,"y":[[0,1,1],[1,0,1]],"y_safestan_flat":[0,1,1,1,0,1]}","protected_variables":["y_safestan_flat"]}
